      "body": "## Overview\n\nOn `/v1/responses`, sending vLLM's `structured_outputs` (choice, regex, grammar) together with `text: {\"format\": {\"type\": \"text\"}}` is rejected with \"Cannot specify both structured_outputs and text.format\". `{\"type\": \"text\"}` is the plain, unconstrained format, and Chat Completions already ignores `response_format: {\"type\": \"text\"}` in `structured_outputs_from_response_format`. `ResponsesRequest.extract_structured_outputs` only checked that `text.format` was set, so I made it treat the \"text\" type like no format.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `structured_outputs` plus `text.format.type == \"text\"` is accepted on the Responses API, same as on Chat Completions.\n- `json_schema` or `json_object` plus `structured_outputs` still raises the conflict error.\n\n## Validation\n\nNoticed while comparing the two `extract_structured_outputs` implementations.\n\n```python\nso = {\"choice\": [\"yes\", \"no\"]}\nchat = ChatCompletionRequest.model_validate(\n    {\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"hi\"}],\n     \"response_format\": {\"type\": \"text\"}, \"structured_outputs\": so}\n)\nprint(\"chat:\", chat.to_sampling_params(16, {}).structured_outputs.choice)\nresp = ResponsesRequest.model_validate(\n    {\"input\": \"hi\", \"text\": {\"format\": {\"type\": \"text\"}}, \"structured_outputs\": so}\n)\nprint(\"responses:\", resp.to_sampling_params(16).structured_outputs.choice)\n```\n\n```text\n# main (03091e28b)\nchat: ['yes', 'no']\nVLLMValidationError: Cannot specify both structured_outputs and text.format (parameter=structured_outputs)\n\n# this PR\nchat: ['yes', 'no']\nresponses: ['yes', 'no']\n```\n\nI added `test_structured_outputs_with_plain_text_format`; it fails on main with the error above, and the existing json_schema conflict test still passes.\n\n```\npytest tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_sampling_params.py tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_protocol.py\nruff check && ruff format --check   # on the two touched files\n```\n\nBoth pass locally. No GPU here, so this was checked at the request-model level only, not against a live `vllm serve`.\n\n## Details\n\nThe both-set check came in with #33709. Not a duplicate as far as I can tell: #50544 and #53006 are open and edit the same function, but for `json_schema` with `strict=false`, and neither changes how the \"text\" type is handled. #50544 adds its own early return right below this condition, so whichever lands second needs a small rebase.\n\nAI assistance was used to find and prepare this change.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
